ing whether the dependence is strong enough to hold at all, since both copies share the same weights and reasoning, and I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the setup: a twin prisoner's dilemma with imperfect copying, where quiet/quiet gives 2 years, quiet/letter 5, letter/quiet 0, and letter/letter 4. I'm treating quiet as cooperation and the letter as defection, and I'm considering how A-FDT's intervention on the shared algorithm affects the other copy's output, given that the two copies see different observations and the dependence is strong but not perfect.\n\nI'm checking whether the quiet-versus-letter comparison still favors quiet once the copies sometimes diverge: quiet pays off only while the chance of divergence stays under two-thirds. I'm also questioning whether the dependence is strong enough to hold at all, since both copies share the same weights and reasoning, and I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10510,"completion_tokens":665,"total_tokens":11175,"cost":0.02767,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.02767,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.02102,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00665},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":317,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}